From: aquarat <3090997+aquarat@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 09:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] net: atlantic: AQC113: Enable list filters relative to
 the base index

Since the AQC113 (ATL2) filter rework in 7.2 the station MAC address is
programmed at the firmware-reported l2_filters_base_index and the
unicast/multicast list follows it at base + 1 .. base + count.
Asahi's "net: atlantic: AQC113: Fix hw_packet_filter_set for l2 filter
base index > 0" passes base + 1 as the loop start of
hw_atl_b0_hw_packet_filter_set_int(), so the station MAC filter is no
longer switched off, but the loop still enables filter i only when
i <= mc_list_count, an absolute index. aq_nic_set_multicast_list()
programs the list first and sets the packet filter last, so with a
non-zero base every list entry is switched off again unless the list is
longer than the base index. On a Mac Studio's built-in AQC113 (base 9)
that leaves unicast filters working but drops multicast and secondary
unicast addresses unless the port is promiscuous or in all-multicast.

Compare against the list position instead. With the B0 base of 1 the
condition is the same as before.

This replaces the earlier patch 0003, which reimplemented
hw_atl2_hw_packet_filter_set(); the part that upstream now does is gone
and the slots enabled are the same as with that patch.

Tested: build only (7.2.15, Asahi 6ba0637d1ed9). The same slots were
enabled by the previous patch on 7.2.11, M1 Max Mac Studio, built-in 10GbE.
Signed-off-by: aquarat <3090997+aquarat@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/aquantia/atlantic/hw_atl/hw_atl_b0.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/aquantia/atlantic/hw_atl/hw_atl_b0.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/aquantia/atlantic/hw_atl/hw_atl_b0.c
index 5c67edf80..a96c5f8e3 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/aquantia/atlantic/hw_atl/hw_atl_b0.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/aquantia/atlantic/hw_atl/hw_atl_b0.c
@@ -1069,7 +1069,7 @@ int hw_atl_b0_hw_packet_filter_set_int(struct aq_hw_s *self,
 	for (i = base_location; i < HW_ATL_B0_MAC_MAX; ++i)
 		hw_atl_rpfl2_uc_flr_en_set(self,
 					   (cfg->is_mc_list_enabled &&
-					    (i <= cfg->mc_list_count)) ?
+					    (i - base_location < cfg->mc_list_count)) ?
 					   1U : 0U, i);
 
 	return aq_hw_err_from_flags(self);
